```

---

## 21. Check active input shaper settings

SSH into the Raspberry Pi and run:

```bash
cd ~/printer_data/logs
```

```bash
grep -A8 "\[input_shaper\]" klippy.log | head -n 20
```

or:

```bash
grep -Ei "shaper_freq|input shaper" klippy.log | tail -n 20
```

In the Klipper console, you can also run:

```gcode
SET_INPUT_SHAPER
```

This reads back the current input shaper settings.

---

Finally a full reboot recomended:

```bash
sudo reboot
```

